From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - The text shape readers take no more than their buffer holds, and
 stop at a stream that has failed

BRepTools::Read of a text BREP that is cut short, or damaged, faulted or never returned. Three
defects, all in code that assumes an extraction succeeded.

An unbounded read into a char array. BRepTools_ShapeSet, TopTools_ShapeSet, TopTools_LocationSet,
GeomTools_SurfaceSet, GeomTools_CurveSet, GeomTools_Curve2dSet, Poly and BinTools_ShapeSet each
read a token with IS >> buffer into a char[255] (char[100] in Poly). The token is written whole,
so a 400 byte word in place of a section name or a shape type overwrote the stack. The reads now
carry the size of the buffer (std::setw), as BinTools already does for the name of a table.

GeomTools::GetReal reads a number into 32 characters, since the change that shrank its buffer from
256. A number of 32 characters or more was cut, and its tail was read as the next number: the
tokens of the record moved by one, and BRepTools::Read faulted or never returned (OCCT#1560). The
rest of a cut number is now taken from the stream before the value is converted.

A stale value after a failed extraction. After a failed extraction a variable keeps what it held,
or is uninitialised, and the readers went on to use it:
 - TopTools_ShapeSet::Read indexed the shape table with atoi of the previous token,
   myShapes(nbshapes - atoi(buffer + 1) + 1), unchecked (the library is built with No_Exception,
   so the range check of NCollection_IndexedMap::operator() is gone). A reference the file made up
   did the same. The token, the location after it and the type of a shape are now checked for a
   failed stream, and the index for the range of the table.
 - The vertex and edge loops of BRepTools_ShapeSet::ReadGeometry, do { IS >> val; ... } while
   (val > 0), never ended when the stream failed, because val kept its last value (OCCT#1608).
   They throw when the extraction fails.
 - The count of each table (Locations, Curve2ds, Curves, Surfaces, Polygon3D,
   PolygonOnTriangulations, Triangulations) ran to its declared count on a stream that had
   failed, up to 2^31 iterations; each loop now stops, and the name of a table is checked for a
   failed read before it is compared. TopTools_LocationSet::Read checked nothing of the location
   it composes with (myMap(l1)): it is now looked up only when it is in the table.
 - A B-spline curve or surface cut short was built from knots and multiplicities that were never
   read, and the constructor indexed with them. It is not built when the stream has failed.
 - The curve or surface under a trimmed or offset curve, an extrusion, a revolution or a trimmed
   or offset surface was passed to the constructor when its own read had given nothing. The
   result is left null and the stream failed.

A well-formed file is read as before. Failure is reported the way these readers already report
it: Standard_Failure from TopTools_ShapeSet::Read and BRepTools_ShapeSet::ReadGeometry, a null
curve or surface from the Geom readers.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3490, follow-up to #3487 and #3489. Upstream: OCCT#1560,
OCCT#1608.

